MEMO

TO:

Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins, City of Cheyenne

City Council Members

FROM:
Thomas D. Cobb, PE, City Engineer

DATE:
August 14, 2023

SUBJECT:
Cooperative Agreement between Wyoming Department of Transportation and
the City of Cheyenne

Project ARSCT N561A02

US 30/ Pershing Boulevard to Christensen Road Cheyenne Streets, Laramie
County

Please find the attached the proposed Cooperative Agreement for Federal Project No. ARSCT
N561A02, US 30/ Pershing Boulevard to Christensen Road Cheyenne Streets in Laramie County
provided by WYDOT to the City of Cheyenne for your approval and execution.  The agreement is
summarized below for your information.

Purpose of Project:
A multi-disciplinary, multi-entity (Cheyenne MPO, City of Cheyenne, WYDOT, and Laramie County)
study of the US 30 Corridor concluded in 2020. The study resulted in a recommendation and
preliminary design for US 30 US 30 (Pershing Boulevard to Christensen Road).  The study
recommended project improvements in the corridor to support planned growth in the southeast
portion of the Cheyenne urban area. That growth is occurring, and traffic volume is increasing as
expected.  More details on the purpose and need are available through the Cheyenne MPO’s
website:

https://www.plancheyenne.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/East-Dell-Report-Final-Online.pdf

Purpose of Agreement:
In summary the primary purpose of the agreement is to set forth the terms and conditions by the
City shall agree to reimburse WYDOT for its share of actual costs incurred to the project, less
previous payments, within forty-five (45) days after billing.

Upon completion and acceptance of the project by WYDOT and the City, the City shall maintain, at
its sole expense, the roadways in compliance with all applicable federal and state standards and
regulations.   Mainteance shall include all repairs necessary to keep the improvements in their

A COMMUNITY OF CHOICE

CITY ENGINEER’S OFFICE
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
