Responsibilities:
City of Cheyenne.
▪
Submit a letter designating a qualified project representative at no cost to WYDOT capable
of authorizing to make timely decisions concerning the project.
▪
Obligated financially contribution as outlined in Exhibit B for the following elements:
o Eleven (11) percent of the Total Direct Costs for Indirect Cost Allocation Plan (ICAP)
associated with overhead expenditures for administering a project by WYDOT.
o Obligated financially for ten (10) percent each of the estimated construction cost for
Construction Engineering and Preliminary Engineering.
▪
If the actual costs exceed twenty (20) percent of the total estimated costs, both parties
agree upon and sign and amendment for the additional costs.
▪
Approve final plans and estimates prior to advertisement by WYDOT.
▪
Upon completion of the project and acceptance by WYDOT, the City shall maintain, at is sole
expense, all features constructed under this agreement.  Maintenance shall include all
repairs necessary to keep improvement in its functional constructed condition.
▪
Once the Acceptance Certificate has been completed, the City shall be responsible for all
storm water runoff on the project and storm water monitoring until a Notic of Termination
(NOT) can NPDES and monitoring.
WYDOT.

▪
WYDOT will conduct preliminary survey work, engineering investigations, National
Environmental Policy Act (NEPA) Compliance and right-of-way studies and will develop
final design plans and estimates for widening Christensen Road north of US 30, pedestrian
underpass lighting, decorative concrete placement in US 30 median, removal of existing
Greenway including low flow barrier walls, electrical, pumps, etc. and new Greenway path.
▪
WYDOT will perform construction engineering for this project in accordance with project
plans and specifications.
▪
WYDOT will advertise this project and award a bid to the lowest qualified bidder in
accordance with WYDOT policies.

Estimated Cost:
The Total City Portion of the project including construction administration and construction cost
estimated by WYDOT is $1,198,800 and $2,080,000 for the Pedestrian Underpass.    Total cost
anticipated at $1,198,800 from the Optional One Percent Sales Tax (2023 – 2026) 5th Penny and
($2,080,000 - $461,169 = $1,618,831; say, $1,625,000) for the 6th Penny Specific Purpose Tax per
separate CSA agreement City Contract #7326.
