immunity shall be construed in favor of immunity.
V.
Taxes. The City shall pay all taxes and other such amounts required by federal,
state, and local law, including, but not limited to, federal and social security taxes,
workers' compensation, unemployment insurance, and sales taxes.
W.
Termination of Agreement. This Agreement may be terminated, without cause,
by WYDOT upon thirty (30) days written notice. This Agreement may be
terminated by WYDOT immediately for cause if the City fails to perform in
accordance with the terms of this Agreement. If at any time during the performance
of this Agreement, in the opinion of WYDOT, the work is not progressing
satisfactorily or within the tenns of this Agreement, then, at the sole discretion of
WYDOT and after written notice to the City, WYDOT may terminate this
Agreement or any part of it. As of the termination date, the City will be entitled to
a pro rata payment for all work accomplished and accepted by WYDOT; however,
the City shall be liable to WYDOT for the entire cost of replacement services for
the duration of the Agreement term.
X.
